08-every-image-has-a-row: favicon gone, every image checked, one alt line per photo, test photos served with no name

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 3a60ab0..397c52b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ FAIR: findable through a Library entry in their sandbox and a public repository;
 
 ## Data and photo rights
 
-Code is MIT (`LICENSE`). Our own photos and copy are CC BY 4.0. A photograph from somewhere else keeps its own licence: we take CC0, public domain, and CC BY or CC BY-SA at 2.0, 3.0 or 4.0, recorded at the exact version and never rounded up. Every image has a row in `photos/manifest.csv` with its source, author and licence, and every photograph a visitor can see is named with its author on `/credits`, which is what CC BY asks for. The web build refuses to run if a photograph that needs an author does not have one. No AI-generated images anywhere; no faces, house numbers or plates. The usability test is anonymous and the creek check is pseudonymous; `docs/DATA_HANDLING.md` says what is stored and what the hosts log on their own. Third-party dependencies and licences: `docs/THIRD_PARTY.md`.
+Code is MIT (`LICENSE`). Our own photos and copy are CC BY 4.0. A photograph from somewhere else keeps its own licence: we take CC0, public domain, and CC BY or CC BY-SA at 2.0, 3.0 or 4.0, recorded at the exact version and never rounded up. Every photograph has a row in `photos/manifest.csv` with its source, author, licence and a plain alt line. On a photo someone answers about, the alt line never names what the question asks. The only other images in the repository are our own screenshots and charts, and the marked lesson sheets in `docs/screens/marks/`, which print the author and licence of their photo. `scripts/check_manifest.py` fails on any other image anywhere in the tree, and the web build fails on any image it would serve without a row. Every photograph a visitor can see is named with its author on `/credits`, which is what CC BY asks for. A test photo reaches the browser under a name that says nothing and with no source link, because its file name and source page would give the answer away. The web build refuses to run if a photograph that needs an author does not have one. No AI-generated images anywhere; no faces, house numbers or plates. The usability test is anonymous and the creek check is pseudonymous; `docs/DATA_HANDLING.md` says what is stored and what the hosts log on their own. Third-party dependencies and licences: `docs/THIRD_PARTY.md`.
 
